Looking at this problem, I need to find the chromatic polynomial of a unicyclic graph, count odd coefficients mod 2 using Lucas' theorem, and minimize.

## Setup

A Type-$k$ Stable Configuration is a connected graph on 2017 vertices with 2017 edges and a unique cycle of length $k$ — i.e., a **unicyclic graph** with cycle $C_k$ and trees attached to cycle vertices.

**Chromatic polynomial.** For a unicyclic graph with cycle $C_k$ and trees $T_1,\dots,T_k$ attached (where $T_i$ includes cycle vertex $v_i$, and $\sum|T_i|=2017$): coloring the cycle gives $P_{C_k}(x)=(x-1)^k+(-1)^k(x-1)$, then each tree contributes $(x-1)^{|T_i|-1}$ given $v_i$'s color. So:

$$P_G(x)=\bigl((x-1)^k+(-1)^k(x-1)\bigr)\cdot(x-1)^{2017-k}=(x-1)^{2017}+(-1)^k(x-1)^{2018-k}$$

## Counting odd coefficients

Set $n=2017$, $m=2018-k$. The coefficient of $x^j$ is $c_j=\binom{n}{j}(-1)^{n-j}+(-1)^k\binom{m}{j}(-1)^{m-j}$. Mod 2, signs vanish:

$$c_j \equiv \binom{n}{j}+\binom{m}{j}\pmod{2}$$

By **Lucas' theorem**, $\binom{a}{j}$ is odd iff $j\subseteq a$ (submask in binary). Let $S_a=\{j:j\subseteq a\}$. The number of odd coefficients is $|S_n\triangle S_m|$:

$$V(m)=2^{\text{pc}(n)}+2^{\text{pc}(m)}-2\cdot 2^{\text{pc}(n\,\&\,m)}$$

where pc = popcount.

**Binary:** $2017=11111100001_2$ with bits at positions $\{10,9,8,7,6,5,0\}$, so $\text{pc}(2017)=7$ and $|S_{2017}|=128$.

$$V(m)=128+2^{\text{pc}(m)}-2^{1+\text{pc}(2017\,\&\,m)}$$

## Minimizing $V(m)$

**Case 1: $m\subseteq 2017$ (submask).** Then $2017\,\&\,m=m$, so $V(m)=128+2^{\text{pc}(m)}-2^{1+\text{pc}(m)}=128-2^{\text{pc}(m)}$.

To minimize, maximize $\text{pc}(m)$. The only 7-bit submask is $2017$ itself, but $m=2018-k\le 2015$ (since $k\ge 3$), so $2017$ is excluded. The maximum achievable is $\text{pc}(m)=6$, giving $V=128-64=64$.

**Case 2: $m\not\subseteq 2017$.** Then $\text{pc}(2017\,\&\,m)\le\text{pc}(m)-1$, so $V(m)\ge 128+2^{\text{pc}(m)}-2^{\text{pc}(m)}=128>64$.

Therefore $t=64$, achieved exactly when $m$ is a 6-bit submask of 2017 with $m\le 2015$.

## Finding all valid $b$

The 6-bit submasks of $2017=11111100001_2$ are obtained by removing one bit from $\{10,9,8,7,6,5,0\}$:

| Removed bit (value) | $m=2017-\text{val}$ | $b=2018-m$ | Valid? |
|---|---|---|---|
| bit 0 (1) | 2016 | 2 | No ($b<3$) |
| bit 5 (32) | 1985 | **33** | Yes |
| bit 6 (64) | 1953 | **65** | Yes |
| bit 7 (128) | 1889 | **129** | Yes |
| bit 8 (256) | 1761 | **257** | Yes |
| bit 9 (512) | 1505 | **513** | Yes |
| bit 10 (1024) | 993 | **1025** | Yes |

Each valid $b\in[3,2017]$ corresponds to an achievable Type-$b$ configuration (attach a path of length $2017-b$ to one cycle vertex).

## Sum

$$33+65+129+257+513+1025=2022$$

